I’m not the one who speaks the most,
Or shares my feelings like a post.
But when I find a friend who’s true,
I slowly open up to you.

I treasure moments, big and small,
The random talks, the midnight calls.
The coffee dates, the games we play,
The little things that make my day.

I may not always show I care,
Or find the perfect words to share.
But deep inside, I hope you know,
You’re more important than I show.

I know that life can change its ways,
And take us through some distant days.
But even when we’re far apart,
You’ll always have a place in my heart.

I don’t need friends who shine like gold,
Or promises that won’t grow old.
Just honest hearts that choose to stay,
And bring me smiles along the way.

So if you ask what friendship means,
It’s shared laughter and familiar scenes.
It’s having people who make life worthwhile,
And finding comfort in every smile.
